{
  "id": "COMPOUND:38301 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Hedaol B is implicated in the interaction with DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular targets. The evidence suggests that Hedaol B acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 3Beta-[(Alpha-Larabinopyranosyl)Oxy]-23-Oxo-Olean-12-En-28-Oic Acid, Marsdenoside K, and (-)-Bisdechlorogeodin, all of which are known to target DNA polymerase iota. These compounds are likely acting as modulators or inhibitors of DNA polymerase iota, thereby establishing a pathway through which Hedaol B may influence its activity. The presence of multiple distinct targets for Hedaol B, each leading to DNA polymerase iota, indicates a potential mechanism of action that involves the modulation of DNA polymerase iota activity. The integration of these findings highlights the role of Hedaol B in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota, possibly through the action of these compounds, and underscores the importance of Hedaol B in the context of DNA polymerase iota regulation.",
